Looking at the comment, I need to express: if the index is valid, every element after the removed position is shifted left by one.

- "index is valid": `0 <= index && index < \old(this.size())`
- "every element after the removed position": positions `i` from `index` to `\old(size)-2`
- "shifted left by one": `this.get(i)` equals the old element at `i+1`

<code>assert (0 <= index && index < \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size())-1; this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment: "If the index is valid, every element after the removed position is shifted left by one, preserving the original order."

This means: premise that index is valid (between 0 and old size), and then for every position from the removed index up to the new size, the element now equals the element that was originally one position to the right.

<code>assert (index>=0 && index<\old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
